<title>GERMANY: Allianz life unit upbeat for 1997.</title>
<headline>Allianz life unit upbeat for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allianz Lebensversicherungs AG, the life insurance unit of Allianz AG Holding, said on Thursday it was optimistic about 1997 and expected business to develop satisfactorily.</p>
<p>The insurer said its group premium income rose by 3.8 percent to about 12 billion marks ($7.1 billion) in 1996 and that new business had shown brisk growth, with new premium income up 9.8 percent to 2.5 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.684 German Marks)</p>
